### Spring Security authorization exercise - manual requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# Start the application first (./mvnw spring-boot:run). All demo passwords are "password".
# "Expected after the exercise" notes describe the target behaviour once the TODOs are done.
# In the starter state every request below succeeds (2xx), which is exactly the problem.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Products - anonymous (expected after the exercise: 200)
GET {{host}}/api/products

### 2a. Report - anonymous (expected after the exercise: 401)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/reports

### 2b. Report - alice / CUSTOMER (expected after the exercise: 403)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/reports
Authorization: Basic alice password

### 2c. Report - manager / MANAGER (expected after the exercise: 403)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/reports
Authorization: Basic manager password

### 2d. Report - admin / ADMIN (expected after the exercise: 200)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/reports
Authorization: Basic admin password

### 3a. Create order - anonymous (starter: owner "guest"; expected after the exercise: 401)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"productId": 1, "quantity": 1}

### 3b. Create order - alice (expected: 201, ownerUsername "alice")
# The ownerUsername field is ignored: the owner always comes from the authenticated user.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Basic alice password
Content-Type: application/json

{"productId": 2, "quantity": 2, "ownerUsername": "bob"}

### 3c. Create order - invalid data (expected: 400)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Basic alice password
Content-Type: application/json

{"productId": 99, "quantity": 0}

### 4a. Read order 101 - alice, the owner (expected after the exercise: 200)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/101
Authorization: Basic alice password

### 4b. Read order 101 - bob, not the owner (expected after the exercise: 403)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/101
Authorization: Basic bob password

### 4c. Read order 101 - admin (expected after the exercise: 200)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/101
Authorization: Basic admin password

### 4d. Read order 101 - anonymous (expected after the exercise: 401)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/101

### 4e. Read a missing order - admin (expected: 404)
GET {{host}}/api/orders/999
Authorization: Basic admin password

### 5a. Cancel order 102 - bob / CUSTOMER, the owner (expected after the exercise: 403)
DELETE {{host}}/api/orders/102
Authorization: Basic bob password

### 5b. Cancel order 102 - manager (expected after the exercise: 204)
DELETE {{host}}/api/orders/102
Authorization: Basic manager password

### 5c. Cancel order 103 - admin (expected after the exercise: 204)
DELETE {{host}}/api/orders/103
Authorization: Basic admin password

### 6a. Refund order 101 - refund-agent / ORDER_REFUND (expected after the exercise: 204)
# Supporting endpoint (not part of the original exercise spec).
POST {{host}}/api/orders/101/refund
Authorization: Basic refund-agent password

### 6b. Refund order 101 - admin, who has no ORDER_REFUND (expected after the exercise: 403)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/101/refund
Authorization: Basic admin password

### 6c. Refund order 101 - alice, the owner (expected after the exercise: 403)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/101/refund
Authorization: Basic alice password

### 7a. [Bonus] Status PROCESSING - manager (expected after the bonus: 204)
# Supporting endpoint (not part of the original exercise spec).
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/101/status
Authorization: Basic manager password
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "PROCESSING"}

### 7b. [Bonus] Status SHIPPED - manager (expected after the bonus: 204)
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/101/status
Authorization: Basic manager password
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "SHIPPED"}

### 7c. [Bonus] Status CANCELLED - manager (expected after the bonus: 403)
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/101/status
Authorization: Basic manager password
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "CANCELLED"}

### 7d. [Bonus] Status CANCELLED - admin (expected after the bonus: 204)
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/101/status
Authorization: Basic admin password
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "CANCELLED"}

### 7e. [Bonus] Status SHIPPED - alice / CUSTOMER (expected after the bonus: 403)
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/101/status
Authorization: Basic alice password
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "SHIPPED"}

### 7f. [Bonus] Unknown status - admin (starter: 400; after the bonus, the outcome depends on your rule)
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/101/status
Authorization: Basic admin password
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "LOST"}
